## Flares and fatigue

Agree a **flare plan** with your IBD team, and contact them early if symptoms start. Pace yourself, and plan rest.

## Food

There is no one diet for IBD. Some people find certain foods make symptoms worse during a flare. Keep a food diary, and talk to a dietitian before cutting out whole food groups.

## Stop smoking

Smoking makes **Crohn's disease** worse and treatments less effective. Your local stop smoking service can help for free.

## Toilet access

- a **Radar key** opens thousands of locked accessible toilets. See [accessible toilets](/support/leisure/accessible-toilets/)
- a **"Can't Wait" card** from Crohn's and Colitis UK or Bladder and Bowel UK can help you ask to use a toilet in shops and cafes

## Travel

Plan toilet stops, carry a spare change of clothes, and take extra medicine. Check if your medicines need to be kept cool.

## Mental health

Anxiety and depression are more common with IBD. Talk to your team or GP if you are struggling.

## Support

**Crohn's and Colitis UK** has a helpline and local networks. **Colostomy UK** and the **IA** (Ileostomy and Internal Pouch Association) support people with stomas.
